# VVDN -- Take-off Clearance Trigger Point demo, RWY 35R, real Gate 26.
# Implements the ONE fully-confirmed trigger point from
# FTS Server/docs/VVDN-Trigger-Point-Consecutive-Departures.docx:
#   HEAVY leads -> MEDIUM follows: minimum = 120s (ICAO Doc 4444 Sec.5.8.3.1(3),
#   "LIGHT or MEDIUM aircraft taking off behind a HEAVY aircraft -- 2 minutes").
#   Worst-case real HEAVY type (B773, furthest of B788/A332/B773 at t=120s per
#   headless BADA simulation) reaches 6.065 NM / ~1984 ft along the RWY 35R
#   centerline (true heading 352.10 deg) at that moment -- this is P_wake.
#
# UNLIKE the earlier VVDN_GATE28_6DEP file (fixed time-offset schedule with
# MOVE-approximated ground/climb physics), this file:
#  (a) uses the PROVEN, real-BADA-driven taxi/roll/climb technique from
#      "VVDN 2026-08-10_08-06-28 (ban 40) - Copy/VVDN_KB5_1HOUR_MIXED.scn"
#      (CRE + ADDWPT + LNAV/VNAV ON, MOVE used ONLY for a true full stop at
#      hold, never during taxi/roll/climb) -- see _TRIGGERDEMO_*.scn helper
#      files in this same folder, copied verbatim from that reference;
#  (b) releases the FOLLOWING aircraft's actual takeoff roll via a genuine
#      geographic ATDIST trigger on the LEADING aircraft's position (P_wake),
#      not a fixed time gap -- exactly the "Take-off Clearance Trigger Point"
#      the source docx asks for.
#
# DEP_LEAD = B773 (HEAVY, real fuselage length 73.9m for TAXION separation).
# DEP_FOLL = A320 (MEDIUM, real fuselage length 37.57m), CRE +60s later at the
# same real Gate 26 (16.052628,108.201989) -- taxis in trail and holds short
# of RWY 35R (via STOP_HOLD) well before DEP_LEAD reaches P_wake; its
# take-off roll is released ONLY when DEP_LEAD crosses P_wake.
#
# P_wake trigger implementation note: ATDIST's third argument is a target
# DISTANCE VALUE relative to the given point (bluesky/traffic/conditional.py
# atdistcmd -- it fires when the aircraft's distance-to-point crosses that
# value), NOT a fixed marker coordinate with a proximity radius. An earlier
# version of this file targeted a separately-computed lat/lon "6.065NM along
# the runway heading" with a small tolerance -- live headless testing showed
# DEP_LEAD's REAL flown track (via the real PAPRA SID waypoints, which does
# not retrace a perfectly straight extension of the runway centerline) never
# came within that tolerance, so the trigger never fired. Fixed by using the
# real RWY 35R threshold itself (16.0290376, 108.202528, VVDN.json
# "verified") as the ATDIST reference point with target distance 6.065 --
# this fires exactly when DEP_LEAD's distance FROM THE THRESHOLD (its actual
# flown distance, along whatever track it is really on) reaches 6.065 NM,
# matching the P_wake definition in the docx exactly and independent of the
# exact lateral track shape.

00:00:00.00>PLUGINS LOAD SURFACETAXI
00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS ON
00:00:00.00>PAN 16.0400,108.2000

# ============ DEP_LEAD -- B773 (HEAVY), first departure, rolls straight out ============
00:00:00.00>CRE DEP_LEAD,B773,16.052628,108.201989,80.9,0,15
00:00:00.00>PCALL _TRIGGERDEMO_TAXI_G26_RWYHOLD DEP_LEAD
00:00:00.00>TAXION DEP_LEAD 15 73.9
# first departure, nobody to wait for -> snap exactly onto the real
# threshold/heading (352.10deg true, VVDN.json "verified"), then roll
# straight through -- without this exact lineup the climb-out route would
# begin from whatever position/heading the taxi ADDWPT chain left it at,
# which is not guaranteed to sit precisely on the RWY 35R centerline.
00:00:00.00>DEP_LEAD ATDIST 16.029200,108.202500,0.01 PCALL _TRIGGERDEMO_LINEUP_AND_ROLL DEP_LEAD 16.0290376 108.202528 352.10
# P_wake trigger: once DEP_LEAD's distance FROM THR 35R reaches 6.065NM,
# release DEP_FOLL's own take-off roll (ICAO 4444 5.8.3.1(3), 120s HEAVY->MEDIUM)
00:00:00.00>DEP_LEAD ATDIST 16.0290376,108.202528,6.065 PCALL _TRIGGERDEMO_DEP_ROLL DEP_FOLL

# ============ DEP_FOLL -- A320 (MEDIUM), taxis in trail, holds short, ============
# ============ take-off roll gated on DEP_LEAD crossing P_wake ============
00:01:00.00>CRE DEP_FOLL,A320,16.052628,108.201989,80.9,0,15
00:01:00.00>PCALL _TRIGGERDEMO_TAXI_G26_RWYHOLD DEP_FOLL
00:01:00.00>TAXION DEP_FOLL 15 37.57
00:01:00.00>DEP_FOLL ATDIST 16.029200,108.202500,0.01 PCALL _TRIGGERDEMO_STOP_HOLD DEP_FOLL 16.029200 108.202500 352.1
